--TEST--
`+ - * / % **` refuse every operand `rule:types/arithmetic` gives no arithmetic row for, and `%` refuses a `float` at both ends — `rule:types/arithmetic`, `rule:types/conversion`, `rule:types/arithmetic`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:types/arithmetic`'s arithmetic rows name the numeric types and nothing else, the
// same way its ordering row does. Everything PHP adds beyond them it adds by
// converting an operand first, and `rule:types/conversion` has no implicit conversion for
// that to be — so each line below is one absent row, and each help names the
// spelling that says what was meant instead.
enum Mode { Read, Write }

class Cell { public int $n = 1; }

bool $flag = true;
string $s = "12";
bytes $raw = "ab" as bytes;
array<int> $xs = [1, 2];
Mode $mode = Mode::Read;
Cell $cell = new Cell();
float $f = 7.5;
int $i = 2;

// `bool` is the operand this refusal exists for: it is PHP's "convert to an
// `int` first", and unrefused it did not even answer PHP's number.
mixed $a = $flag + $flag;
mixed $b = $flag ** $flag;
// Two strings combine with `.`, and become numbers with `as`.
mixed $c = $s - $s;
// An object has no arithmetic at all: Novis has no operator overloading.
mixed $d = $cell * $cell;
// A `bytes` and an `array<T>` are on no row either.
mixed $e = $raw + $raw;
mixed $g = $xs / $xs;
// An enum value has a diagnostic of its own, the one every operator over it reports.
mixed $h = $mode * $mode;
// `%` is the one refusal both operands are numbers for: PHP converts to an
// integer and answers one, § 4's float row would answer a `float`, and the
// spec makes `Core\Math::mod` the floating-point remainder.
mixed $j = $f % $f;
mixed $k = $f % $i;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0716]: `+` has no meaning for `bool`
%A
error[E0716]: `**` has no meaning for `bool`
%A
error[E0716]: `-` has no meaning for `string`
%A
error[E0716]: `*` has no meaning for `Cell`
%A
error[E0716]: `+` has no meaning for `bytes`
%A
error[E0716]: `/` has no meaning for `array<int>`
%A
error[E0415]: `*` has no meaning for `Mode`
%A
error[E0717]: `%` has no meaning for `float`
%A
error[E0717]: `%` has no meaning for `float`
%A
error: aborting due to 9 errors
